Description: Fix ft2font.cpp build with FreeType >= 2.10.2 / strict C++
 FreeType 2.10.2 changed FT_Outline::tags from `char*` to `unsigned char*`.
 Under stricter C++ (e.g. -std=c++17 without -fpermissive), assigning
 `outline.tags + first` to the local `char *tags` variable now fails with:
   error: invalid conversion from 'unsigned char*' to 'char*'
 Cast to char* to restore the previous (well-defined) behavior. FT_CURVE_TAG
 only inspects the low two bits, so signedness of the cast is irrelevant.
Origin: backport, https://github.com/matplotlib/matplotlib (upstream cast for newer FreeType)
Forwarded: not-needed (matplotlib 2.2.x is end-of-life)
Author: ActiveState build patch
Last-Update: 2026-05-14

--- a/src/ft2font.cpp
+++ b/src/ft2font.cpp
@@ -204,7 +204,7 @@
         v_control = v_start;

         point = outline.points + first;
-        tags = outline.tags + first;
+        tags = (char *)(outline.tags + first);
         tag = FT_CURVE_TAG(tags[0]);

         // A contour cannot start with a cubic control point!
@@ -320,7 +320,7 @@
         v_control = v_start;

         point = outline.points + first;
-        tags = outline.tags + first;
+        tags = (char *)(outline.tags + first);
         tag = FT_CURVE_TAG(tags[0]);

         double x, y;
